From: WS3006 DTS fix
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: reset internal PHYs during mt7531_setup

The MT7531 software reset sequence in mt7531_setup() omits
SYS_CTRL_PHY_RST, unlike MT7530 and AN7583 which both include it.
When no external reset-gpios is available (e.g. shared reset line
designs), the internal PHYs remain in whatever state the bootloader
left them, causing intermittent failures:

- PHY probe validation returning wrong capabilities
- "poll timeout" / "reset timeout" on FDB operations
- "irq XX: nobody cared" from unhandled PHY interrupts
- Link flaps during initial negotiation

Add SYS_CTRL_PHY_RST to the internal software reset, matching the
MT7530 and AN7583 behaviour. For boards with a dedicated reset-gpios,
the PHY reset is redundant but harmless.

This fixes the Huasifei WS3006 which shares a single GPIO reset line
between the MT7531 switch and an RTL8221B external PHY — the switch
cannot claim the GPIO without conflicting with the PHY driver.

Signed-off-by: WS3006 DTS fix
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -2687,7 +2687,9 @@ mt7531_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 		mt7530_write(priv, MT753X_PMCR_P(i), MT7531_FORCE_MODE_LNK);

 	/* Reset the switch through internal reset */
-	mt7530_write(priv, MT7530_SYS_CTRL, SYS_CTRL_SW_RST | SYS_CTRL_REG_RST);
+	mt7530_write(priv, MT7530_SYS_CTRL,
+		     SYS_CTRL_PHY_RST | SYS_CTRL_SW_RST |
+		     SYS_CTRL_REG_RST);

 	if (!priv->p5_sgmii) {
 		mt7531_pll_setup(priv);
